<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Arithmetic Mean and Other Stats Calculation for a Given Dataset 1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the following data set:</p>

<p>{@data@}</p>

<p><em>Note: For the following, submit your answer correct to two decimal places where appropriate.</em></p>

<p>a. Calculate its arithmetic mean: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>b. Calculate its median: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>c. Calculate its standard deviation: [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>d. Calculate its interquartile range: [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Arithmetic mean</strong></p>

<p>The arithmetic mean is given by the formula
\( \displaystyle \bar{x} = \frac{\sum_{i=1}^n x_i}{n}\).</p>

<p>In this case,
\( \displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^n x_i = {@sum(data[i],i,1,20)@}\)
and \(n = 20\). Therefore,
\(\bar{x} = {@disp_mean@}\).</p>


<p><strong>Median</strong></p>

<p>The median is the middle value of an ordered dataset. Since there are \(20\) observations, the median is the arithmetic mean of the 10th and 11th values after the data have been arranged in ascending order.</p>

<p>Therefore, the median of this dataset is
\({@disp_median@}\).</p>


<p><strong>Standard deviation</strong></p>

<p>The population standard deviation is given by the formula
\( \displaystyle \sigma = \sqrt{\frac{\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i-\bar{x})^2}{n}}\).</p>

<p>For this dataset, \(n=20\) and
\(\bar{x}={@disp_mean@}\).</p>

<p>Therefore, the standard deviation is
\(\sigma = {@disp_std@}\).</p>


<p><strong>Interquartile range</strong></p>

<p>The interquartile range is the difference between the third quartile and the first quartile:
\( \displaystyle \mathrm{IQR}=Q_3-Q_1\).</p>

<p>For this dataset,
\(Q_1={@disp_q1@}\) and
\(Q_3={@disp_q3@}\).</p>

<p>Therefore,
\(\mathrm{IQR}={@disp_q3@}-{@disp_q1@}
={@disp_iqr@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
